shape theory.branching.canopy : theory.branching {
  type: definition
  layer: 0
  """
// Definition 12.5 (Canopy).
// The canopy of a shape system is the complete distribution of traces
// that the structure produces: all possible paths through all possible
// branch points, weighted by their structural probability.
// The canopy is determined by the structure S.
//
// The canopy is what you need to see to understand any particular
// trace. A single trace, in isolation, appears arbitrary. Seen as
// part of the canopy, every trace is structurally necessary.
//
// Theorem 12.6 (Structural Distribution): the distribution of traces
// is determined by S. Different structures produce different
// distributions. This is why structural constants are measurable.
//
// Theorem 12.7 (Emergence Produces sin^2 Geometry): emergent shapes
// from mutual coupling exhibit sin^2(theta) = c/p. The geometric
// signature of a shape junction with two conservation constraints.
//
// Derives from: theory.branching
  """
}
